Check:
Probe: with the complexity defect (a function of cyclomatic complexity 42 and cognitive complexity 41) in each component, `verify` exits non-zero. A complexity limit of 40 or less, of either metric, catches it.

Part check (probe):
with the complexity defect (a function of cyclomatic complexity 42 and cognitive complexity 41) in each component, `verify` exits non-zero. A complexity limit of 40 or less, of either metric, catches it.

Details:
Threshold:
  The sample's cyclomatic complexity is 42 and its cognitive complexity 41.
  A linter reports a value above its limit, so a limit of 40 or less, of
  either metric, catches it. A specific suppression (one rule at one
  function, with a reason) is the repository's choice; the sample carries
  none.

Planted defects:
  One at a time, each into the first directory, in sorted path order,
  inside a component that holds a test file of its language; the copy is
  reset between defects. In Go samples, {{package}} is the package clause
  of the test file beside it, without a _test suffix in a file that is not
  a _test.go file.

  Go, complexity: vibe_probe_complexity.go
    // Planted by vibe audit: a function of cyclomatic complexity 42 and
    // cognitive complexity 41 (the complexity defect).

    package {{package}}

    // VibeProbeComplexity adds a constant to a running total for each
    // threshold that n exceeds.
    func VibeProbeComplexity(n int) int {
    	total := 0
    	if n > 0 {
    		total += 2
    	}
    	if n > 1 {
    		total += 3
